      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T16:51:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have no double from API\u0027s perspective. But from developer\u0027s perspective, all the column names are available to them, through at least two approaches:\n1. cursor#getColumnNames will return all of them (both public and hidden columns)\n2. developer can just hard-code the column name to retrieve the values\n\nTo illustrate, a simple Hell-world app is developed which show all hidden fields (at the build DUPLEX_MODE and DATA_NETWORK_TYPE columns are not added yet) are available and can retrieve the value of ServiceState (without any permission). Please go to end of go/service-state-table-cts to check the details.\n\nI leave this common open in case I did not convince you.\nThanks",
